    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0563" n="445" xml:id="pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.12/954: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-13T18:00:00-06:00">August 13, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>310. Department’s 440, August 13, 3 p.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d538-f1"/> Saw
                    Estrada again yesterday. He sees no objection to formula Department’s 435,
                    August 7, 5 p.m. and Embassy’s August 6, 7 p.m. He has not however been able to
                    see President who is out of the city. We will see Estrada again tomorrow and
                    report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
